{"author":{"id":"127a58c7f014820991be95805df42525db12c92e2d7319d04d4df105a9aa3444"},"ops":[{"type":3,"timestamp":1788291605,"nonce":"Oxlx3CEN279Waw6clIUNTnN+fMc=","message":"SESSION 19 HANDOVER — the round that made \"advance until it's done\" sayable.\n\nMerged to `main` fast-forward at `3dc858d`; `Build:` commit stands alone and its\npdb path names the canonical worktree. Working tree clean.\n\n## Closed\n\n- **`fc287ba`** — `advance {until:{condition|layout}}`. Two forms: a predicate\n  over a digest path, and \"every element of this layout is resolved\".\n- **`36999fd`** — `construction {layout_id}` is a real scope, and `--layout_id`\n  is no longer silently binned.\n- **`54b0c9a`** — `short_by` comes from the builder's availability test, not\n  from `map.resourceCounter`.\n\nEach carries a comment answering its acceptance section item by item, including\nthe items NOT met and why.\n\n## The result, in one line\n\n`advance {until:{layout:\"ly-5\"}}` — one call, no tick count — returned 10,255\nticks later with 22 of 22 built and a room the game calls `role: \"Bedroom\"`,\n`proper: true`, `open_roof_cells: 0`. Session 18's \"2000 ticks, look, 6000 more\"\nis gone.\n\n## The finding worth carrying forward\n\n`construction.frames == 0` — the natural spelling of \"wait until the build is\ndone\" — was MEASURED true at the moment 22 blueprints went down, on a room that\ndoes not exist, while the layout scope reported 22 unresolved on the same tick.\nAn edge does not save it either. So the layout form is a named family and not a\npath, and the general rule is in DESIGN's decisions log: **some predicates are\nnot expressible as an operator over a digest path at all.**\n\n## New issue filed, unasked\n\n- **`039e359`** (p2, wave:3, type:spec) — four branches the 140-check suite\n  never reaches: `Materials.unreachable`, a `colonists.list[*]` predicate (the\n  expensive path — so the one number `fc287ba` asks to be measured is measured\n  only on the cheapest path available), `scan_cap`/`unscanned` on a layout over\n  300 live elements, and the `unknown`/`off_map` branches. None is a map-luck\n  gap. Filed because a green number that size reads as coverage it does not\n  have.\n\n## What is unblocked now\n\n`until:{layout}` is the halt `4.2`'s play loop and `4.3`'s ten-day run need to\nstop guessing tick counts, and `until:{condition:{path:\"time.*\"}}` is what makes\ntick arithmetic unnecessary — which retires the accumulated-overshoot worry that\n`overshoot_bound` and `s13-mod-surface` check 3.4 (the permanently-manual one)\nexist to police. Neither is deleted; both stop being load-bearing.\n\nThe same gap is still open for research, bills, plant growth and `61794cd`'s\nbleed clock. NOT closed here, and the surface is shaped so closing them is a\n`StateWatch` subclass plus one parse branch rather than a second mechanism:\n`StateWatch.MatcherKeys`/`OptionKeys` is the whole vocabulary and `TimeDriver`\ndoes not have to learn what a family means.\n\n`261f2e9` (no temperature target) still waits for tiling, per the round brief.\n\n## For whoever runs the bench next\n\n`accept/fc287ba-until-state.py` is the suite (140 checks, phases 0-5; phase 4 is\nslow by construction because it waits for colonists to build a room). Two\nsuite-side facts it learned the hard way and wrote down: the verb registry is\n`status.verbs`, NOT an op called `verbs` — sending it raw answers `unknown-op`,\nwhich is what two of `s13-mod-surface`'s \"missing verb\" failures actually are —\nand `find-rect` spirals from one `near` capped at 20 candidates, so N\nnon-overlapping sites need N probes.","files":null}]}